{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.EmCouplingFixedPoint","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.EmCouplingFixedPoint","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_is_fixed_point_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_is_fixed_point_root","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L160-L179","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on the B₃(ℂ) O(α²) normalization class).**\n\nUnder `AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization q α`, the physical fine-structure\nconstant `α` is a root of the characteristic cubic\n`P(α) = −h²H·α³ + H·α² + T·α − 1` built from the proved tree term\n`q[9]_q[10]_q`, the proved zero-mode `2/(3π)`, and the\n`H = [2]_q/(8π)` normalization, and its inverse is CODATA-consistent.\n\nThe root characterization `alphaCubic q α = 0` is DERIVED from the\nclass' `b3_normalization` field through the sorry-free algebraic\nequivalence `fixedPoint_iff_cubic` — it is not read off a stored\nconclusion field. The CODATA bound is the carried empirical\nhypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:em-coupling-fixed-point","label":"prop:em-coupling-fixed-point","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.codata_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.codata_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L158-L158","doc":"The B₃(ℂ) correction lands the root CODATA-consistently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.b3_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.b3_normalization","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L156-L156","doc":"The conjectural B₃(ℂ) O(α²) normalization: `α` solves the\nself-consistent fixed point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.alpha_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.alpha_pos","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L153-L153","doc":"The candidate physical coupling is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.AlphaEmFixedPointNormalization","kind":"class","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L124-L158","doc":"**B₃(ℂ) O(α²) normalization class** (the sole open input; §3b-cond).\n\nThe class is indexed by the substrate parameter `q` and a candidate\nreal coupling `α`. Its fields carry the *hypotheses* of the\nconditional result — never its conclusion:\n\n· `alpha_pos` — the candidate coupling is positive (so the cubic ⇔\n  fixed-point clearing of `1/α` is valid);\n· `b3_normalization` — the **only** conjectural ingredient: the exact\n  O(α²) self-energy normalization of the fixed point is\n  `H·(1 − h²α)` with `H = [2]_q/(8π)` the archimedean image of a\n  class in the Bloch group `B₃(ℂ)`; equivalently, `α` solves the\n  self-consistency relation `IsAlphaEmFixedPoint q α`. The tree term\n  `q[9]_q[10]_q` and the zero-mode `2/(3π)` are proved sorry-free\n  upstream — they are NOT part of this hypothesis;\n· `codata_consistent` — the B₃(ℂ) correction lands the root at the\n  measured value (the empirical face of the conjecture).\n\nThe class carries HYPOTHESES, not the conclusion: the downstream\ntheorem `alpha_em_is_fixed_point_root` DERIVES `P(α) = 0` from\n`b3_normalization` via `fixedPoint_iff_cubic`, composing the proved\nalgebraic equivalence with the proved upstream pieces. There is no\n`alphaCubic_zero` field to project (non-degenerate per §3b-cond\nitem 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.codataInvAlpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.codataInvAlpha","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L113-L122","doc":"CODATA 2022 value of the inverse fine-structure constant,\n`137.035999177(21)`.\n\nWas the CODATA-2018 Cs-recoil value `137.035999084`. Those are\ndifferent DETERMINATIONS, not merely older digits -- they sit 4.4 sigma\napart on the 2022 uncertainty -- so this was an owner decision rather\nthan a mechanical drain (2026-08-22). The shift is 0.68 ppb against the\n`1e-6` class bound and ~690x smaller than the 468 ppb structural gap the\nCS tower actually carries, so no conclusion here moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.fixedPoint_iff_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.fixedPoint_iff_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L99-L111","doc":"**Genuine derivation (sorry-free).** For any nonzero `α`, the\nself-consistency relation is equivalent to `α` being a root of the\ncharacteristic cubic `P`. This is the algebraic content that lets the\nconditional theorem below DERIVE the polynomial-root characterization\nfrom the B₃(ℂ) fixed-point hypothesis, rather than projecting a stored\nconclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaCubic","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L93-L97","doc":"The characteristic cubic `P(α) = −h²H·α³ + H·α² + T·α − 1`. Its real\npositive root is the physical `α_EM`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.IsAlphaEmFixedPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.IsAlphaEmFixedPoint","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**Self-consistency (fixed-point) relation** for the fine-structure\nconstant at substrate parameter `q`:\n\n  `1/α = T + α·H·(1 − h²·α)`,\n\nwith `T = alphaInvConst q`, `H = habiroNorm q`, `h = hbarQ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L81-L82","doc":"The Habiro deformation parameter `h = (q−1)/q = ℏ_q` (PR #1511). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.habiroNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.habiroNorm","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L74-L79","doc":"Fixed-point normalization coefficient `H = [2]_q/(8π)`. The `8π = π·b₁`\nis the proved harmonic-1-form count on Bring's surface (PR #1552);\nthe identification of the exact O(α²) correction to `H` with a\n`B₃(ℂ)` Bloch class is the sole open input (the class field below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaInvConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alphaInvConst","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L67-L72","doc":"The constant part `T = q·[9]_q·[10]_q + 2/(3π)` of the\nself-consistency relation: the proved tree term plus the proved\nBring zero-mode shift `2/(3π) = bringZeroModeValue` reused from\n`QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.treeInverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.treeInverse","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Tree-level inverse coupling `q·[9]_q·[10]_q` (the sorry-free bare\nformula of `prop:em-coupling-projection`, evaluated on ℝ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.qIntReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.qIntReal","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-fixed-point.lean#L54-L60","doc":"Real q-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)` on the archimedean\n(ℝ) side. Mirrors `q_int` of\n`prop:alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio`; here specialised to `ℝ`\nbecause the fixed-point equation carries the archimedean\ntranscendental `π` and therefore lives past the substrate wall\n(§7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}